    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0057" n="43" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg43"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War, 1939/26585: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-18T13:00:00-04:00">December 18,
                            1942—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2199. Attention Under Secretary and Duggan. Morales United Press interview effect
                    that President Roosevelt expressed the hope to him that President Ríos would
                    make an early visit to the United States has caused general discussion here and
                    the opponents of rupture who by no means have given up the fight are using it to
                    maintain that there is no insistent desire on our part that Chile break
                    relations.</p>
                <p>In this situation I urgently need for my confidential information the cabled
                    indication of the nature of the discussions which I requested in my No. 2184 of
                    December 16, noon.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d54-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
